:SPEAKER Viya
Hey, welcome to daemon.garden.
:YIELD sleep:1000 # set this to autoAdvance
I imagine you have a lot of questions right now. {
    ?: Yes
        -> questions
    ?:^ No \ Nah, not really. (End Conversation)
        -> end
    ?: Battle \ No questions, start a battle with the mimicry please.
        :YIELD battle:MIMICRY # this will set an outcome variable
        [branch]
            [when:outcome=PlayerVictory]
                Wow, nicew job. I'm impressed.
            [when:outcome=OpponentVictory]
                Damn you suck at this. How are you going to survive the fringenet?
            [when:outcome=Draw]
                Close call! Things will only get harder from here...
            [when:outcome=PlayerEject]
                Coward.
                If you're not going to fight, do you at least have some questions? {
                    ?: Yes \ Sure.
                        -> questions
                    ?:^ No (END) \ No, fuck off.
                        -> end
                }
            [unless:outcome]
                idk what happened.
        [/branch]
}

[skip:questions_loopback]
    Any more questions? {
        ?: Yeah
            -> questions
        ?:^ Nah (END Conversation) \ Nah, not really.
            -> end
    }
[/skip]

[skip:questions]
    # get random response from caller: "Go for it.", "I'll try my best.", "Alright."F
    :SIGNAL get_question_prompt
    $question_prompt {
        ?:^ What \ What... {
            ?: Game? \ What is this game?
                @game_exp
                daemon.garden is a point-and-click RPG created by omni.vi
                Episode 0 takes place in the year 2095", "Long after the VI-LINK has become widespread.
                {
                    ?: VI-LINK? \ What is a VI-LINK?
                        The VI-LINK is a neural-interface that allows users to connect to NULLSPACE.
                        -> questions_loopback
                    ?: Cool.
                        Yeah :)
                        -> questions_loopback
                    ?: Lame. \ Sounds boring and LARP-ey.
                        Okay buddy.
                        -> questions_loopback
                }

            ?: This? \ What is this?
                This as in...? {
                    ?: Game \ This game, I mean.
                        -> game_exp
                    ?: Dialogue \ This dialogue system.
                        The dialogue system we're using right now is called Hermes.
                        It was made in-house by omni.
                        It is built on the BunNarraY dialogue scripting language.
                        I like it a lot!
                }
        }

        ?:^ Why \ Why... {
            ?: Game style \ Why does the game look like this?
                Because it looks cool. What kind of question is that?
                -> questions_loopback
        }
    }
[/skip]


@end